use serde_json::Value;

pub fn solve(input: Value) -> Value {
    let input_str = input.as_str().unwrap();
    let mut cents: i64;

    match input_str.parse() {
        Ok(n) => cents = (n * 100.0).round() as i64,
        Err(_) => return Value::Null,
    }

    if cents.abs() > 100000000 {
        return Value::Null;
    }

    Value::Number(cents.into())
}
```

This function takes a `serde_json::Value` as input and returns a `serde_json::Value`. The input is expected to be a string that represents a decimal monetary value. The function converts this string to a 64-bit integer representing the number of cents. If the input string is not a valid decimal number, the function returns `Value::Null`. If the number of cents is greater than 100000000 (1000000 pounds), the function also returns `Value::Null`. Otherwise, the function returns the number of cents as a `Value::Number`.
